## Why this design

**Layout & structure**
- The virtual column is **appended last**, so `columns[0]` keeps meaning "the first real column" — task creation dialogs, `newSprintTask` and `openNewTask` need no changes and can never accidentally target the triage bucket.
- It only exists **while it holds tasks** (`columnList` only yields `NO_COLUMN_ID` when some chat defines no column; `sprintColumns` only pushes it when `tasks.some(t => !t.status)`). Boards with everything classified look identical to before — zero visual noise.

**Interaction**
- Drag **out** of "Unassigned" into a real column writes `chat.column` / `chat.status`.
- Drag **back in** clears the field (`column: ''`, `status: ''`), so the placeholder is never persisted onto a chat.
- `value` vs `title` separation is what makes this safe: the canvas renders `title` ("Unassigned") but every write and comparison uses `value` (`--none--` / `--no-status--`).

**Anti-patterns avoided**
- ❌ Persisting the placeholder: `syncColumnOrder` / `syncSprintColumnOrder` skip `virtual` columns — previously the `--none--` column was written into `board.columns` on the next drag.
- ❌ Editing/creating through a virtual column: `allowCreate`, `allowEdit`, `draggable`, `reorderable` are disabled per column.
- ❌ Cloning chats to default the field: the fallback stays at the comparison sites only (the whole file is built around keeping chat identity stable).

**Accessibility**
- Virtual columns keep the same DOM/order and remain keyboard-reachable through the existing card focus order; the dashed border plus the `fa-circle-question` badge signal "not a real column" without relying on colour alone.

## Verification checklist
- [ ] Kanban board where every chat has a column → no "Unassigned" column appears.
- [ ] Chat with `column: ""` → appears in "Unassigned"; drag it to a real column → persisted; drag it back → `column` cleared.
- [ ] Drag a card from "Unassigned" then reorder columns → `board.columns` contains no `Unassigned`/`--none--` entry.
- [ ] Sprint board with a task whose `status` is empty → "Unassigned" column at the end; dropping it on "Doing" writes `status: doing`.
- [ ] Remove a sprint column → tasks without a status stay in "Unassigned" (they are no longer swept into "To Do").
- [ ] Sidebar shows the board as **Unassigned** with the live count of board-less chats.

