## What you should now see

| Surface | Result |
|---|---|
| Board list (sidebar **Boards** + `KanbanList` overlay) | **Unassigned** row always present, last, with the live count of board-less chats (`0` when there are none) |
| Opening it | Renders `SprintBoardView` in read-only mode (no *New Task*, no *Transfer*, no *Board settings*), columns = canonical statuses + the `Unassigned` column |
| Sprint board canvas | `Unassigned` column always rendered at the end, dashed border + `fa-circle-question` badge |
| Kanban boards | Unchanged: their `Unassigned` column still appears only when a task defines no `column` |

## Behaviour preserved (no regressions)

- **Never persisted** — `syncSprintColumnOrder` and `syncColumnOrder` skip `virtual` columns, so `board.columns` never gains an `Unassigned` entry.
- **Never a creation target** — `newSprintTask` / `newTask` filter `c.virtual`, and the canvas passes `allowCreate`/`allowEdit`/`draggable`/`reorderable` as `false` for virtual columns.
- **Never written onto chats** — dropping back into it calls `moveSprintStatus`, which maps `NO_STATUS_ID → ''` (clears `status`).
- **No new re-renders** — the virtual column pushes plain `{...}` wrappers over the *same* chat objects, so `SprintBoardCanvas.sameColumns` still sees identical cards.

## Verification checklist

- [ ] Project where every chat has a board → **Unassigned** appears in the sidebar with count `0`.
- [ ] Sprint board, all tasks with a status → last column is **Unassigned**, empty, dashed, and has no `+`/edit/grip controls.
- [ ] Add an existing task without a `status` to a sprint → it lands in **Unassigned**.
- [ ] Drag a card from **Unassigned** to *Doing* → `status: doing`; drag it back → `status` cleared, card returns to the bucket.
- [ ] Reorder sprint columns → reload → `board.columns` has no `Unassigned`/`--no-status--` entry and the order is kept.
- [ ] `newSprintTask` (New Task button) still lands in the **first real** column, never in *Unassigned*.

## Known small follow-up (not in this change)

`SprintBoardView` passes the full `columns` array to `SprintBoardModals`. With the virtual column now always present, the dialog's "a board must keep at least one column" guard counts it too (it can enable a *Delete column* click that the store then safely ignores) and a user-chosen column literally named *Unassigned* is rejected as duplicate. Both are cosmetic — passing `columns.filter(c => !c.virtual)` to the modals would remove them if you want me to do it.

