messages.content:
I'll verify how sprint tasks are grouped and rendered before changing the filter.Let me read the sprint board view, the task card, and the chat status helpers.## Diagnosis

The sprint board groups tasks **only by exact `status` equality** with each column:

```js
const columnTasks = tasks.filter(t => (t.status || NO_STATUS_ID) === status)
...
builtColumns.push({ ..., tasks: tasks.filter(t => !t.status) })
```

So the virtual column only collects tasks **without** a status. A task whose `status` is set but not mapped by any column falls in the gap:

| Task `status` | Columns: `todo · doing · done` | Where it renders today |
|---|---|---|
| `''` | — | **Unassigned** ✅ |
| `doing` | matched | Doing ✅ |
| `onhold` / `rejected` (column removed) | no match | **nowhere** ❌ |
| `in_progress` / `pending` / any legacy value | no match | **nowhere** ❌ |

Same happens as soon as a board customizes its columns and drops a status (e.g. keeping only `todo · doing · done` while older tasks still carry `onhold`): those tasks become invisible on the board while still counted nowhere.

## Change

`src/store/kanban.js` — one getter (`sprintColumns`):

- Collect the statuses actually grouped by the board's columns (`builtColumns.map(c => c.status)`, which is exactly `sprintColumnStatus(col)`), then route **everything not in that set** into the virtual column:

```js
const groupedStatuses = new Set(builtColumns.map(col => col.status))
const unclassified = tasks.filter(t => !groupedStatuses.has(t.status)).sort(sortColumnTasks)
```

- `!groupedStatuses.has(t.status)` covers both cases at once (`undefined`/`''` and unknown values), so the previous `!t.status` special case is gone and no task can be listed twice.
- No persistence change: the virtual column stays `virtual: true` and is still skipped by `syncSprintColumnOrder`, `newSprintTask` and the canvas. Dropping a card out of it writes the destination `status`; dropping one back in clears `status` (existing `moveSprintStatus`).

