## Behaviour matrix

| Task `status` | Board columns | Renders in |
|---|---|---|
| `todo` | `todo` exists | To Do ✅ |
| `''` | any | **Unassigned** ✅ |
| `in_progress` (legacy) | `todo · doing · done` | **Unassigned** ✅ *(was invisible)* |
| `onhold` | board kept only `todo · doing · done` | **Unassigned** ✅ *(was invisible)* |
| `doing` | custom column maps `status: "doing"` | that column ✅ |

## Anti-patterns avoided

- ❌ **Rewriting `chat.status` on read.** The bucket is a view-level fallback; the invalid value stays on the chat until the user drags the card, which repairs it.
- ❌ **A second `filter(t => !t.status)`.** Two overlapping filters would let a task be listed twice or not at all; a single `!groupedStatuses.has(t.status)` is exhaustive and mutually exclusive with the real columns.
- ❌ **Deriving valid statuses from `chats.statusList`.** The board's own columns are the source of truth — a custom column can map any status, and the canonical list is only the fallback.

## Accessibility

- The column keeps the same DOM position and card focus order, so keyboard users reach the reclaimed cards with Tab.
- The bucket is signalled by three redundant cues: dashed border, `fa-circle-question` badge and the `Unassigned` label — never colour alone.
- No focusable controls are added (the virtual column keeps `allowCreate`/`allowEdit`/`draggable`/`reorderable` off).

## Verification checklist

- [ ] Task with `status: "onhold"` on a board whose columns are `todo · doing · done` → appears in **Unassigned**.
- [ ] Task with an unknown value (`in_progress`, `pending`, `null`) → appears in **Unassigned**.
- [ ] Drag such a card onto **Doing** → `status: "doing"` persisted, card leaves the bucket.
- [ ] Drag a normal card back into **Unassigned** → `status` cleared (not set to `--no-status--`).
- [ ] Board where every task matches a column → **Unassigned** empty, dashed, no controls.
- [ ] Reorder columns → reload → `board.columns` still has no `Unassigned` / `--no-status--` entry.
- [ ] Counts in `SprintBoardView` (tasks / % done) include the reclaimed cards.

