## Behaviour matrix (after the change)

| Task `status` | Rendered in |
|---|---|
| matches a column (`todo`, `doing`, custom `review`…) | that column |
| `''` / `null` / missing | `Unassigned` (virtual, last) |
| `'blocked'` (no column groups it) | `Unassigned` + warning chip with the raw value |
| same value as a column **and** `_` | never twice — column grouping and triage are mutually exclusive |

## Interaction notes

- **Drag out** of `Unassigned` onto a real column → `moveSprintStatus` writes the destination status (so an unknown status is *fixed* by one drag).
- **Drag into** `Unassigned` → `status` is cleared (`NO_STATUS_ID → ''`); the card stays in the triage bucket and the chip disappears.
- **No persistence** — `boardStatuses` is computed at read time; nothing is ever written onto the chat by the getter.
- **No double render / no new re-renders** — the filter only applies to the virtual column, and the chat objects stay identical, so `SprintBoardCanvas.sameColumns` keeps short-circuiting.

## Verification checklist

- [ ] Sprint board, task with `status: 'blocked'` → card appears in **Unassigned** with the `blocked` chip.
- [ ] Task with a status whose column was removed → appears in **Unassigned**.
- [ ] Task with no status → **Unassigned**, no chip.
- [ ] Drop the `blocked` card on *Doing* → `status: doing`, chip gone, card in *Doing*.
- [ ] Drop it back on **Unassigned** → `status` cleared, card stays there.
- [ ] Reorder columns / reload → `board.columns` has no `Unassigned`/`--no-status--` entry.
- [ ] Header count, progress, stats and cost totals now include the triaged tasks (previously invisible).

